  "planned_workouts": [
    {
      "id": 138555910,
      "date": "2026-09-24",
      "name": "HM-Marathon Threshold 5x2km + Primer",
      "type": "WORKOUT",
      "planned_tss": 93,
      "duration_hours": 1.56,
      "duration_formatted": "1h33m50s",
      "workout_summary": "15m | 5m | 3\u00d720s / 1m10s rec | 2m @162bpm | 3m | 5\u00d78m28s @166bpm / 2m rec | 12m",
      "description": "- Easy warmup 15m Z1 HR, flat route and relaxed stride\n- Progressive warmup 5m Z1-Z2 HR\n\n3x\n- Fast-relaxed activation 20s, smooth cadence and no sprinting\n- Easy jog 70s Z1 HR\n\n- Controlled primer 2m 92-95% LTHR, progress from marathon effort toward lower threshold, RPE 6/10\n- Settle 3m Z1 HR\n\n5x\n- Controlled threshold 2km 94-97% LTHR, RPE 6-7/10, even relaxed form\n- Easy jog recovery 2m Z1 HR\n\n- Easy cooldown 12m Z1 HR\n\nExecution guide: reps 1-2 approximately 3:50-3:47/km. Reps 3-4 may progress toward 3:47-3:45/km if breathing, form and hamstring remain controlled. Rep 5 is completed only if rep 4 remains at RPE no higher than 7/10, pace is stable, HR is no higher than 97% LTHR and the hamstring is unchanged; keep it controlled around 3:47-3:45/km and do not kick. The first 4 reps plus primer approximately match last week's 4x8m drempelbelasting; rep 5 adds progression. Do not chase HR early and do not use aspirational half-marathon pace. Warmup gate: if HR response is abnormal, body feel deteriorates or proximal hamstring pain exceeds 2/10 or changes form, omit the main set and run easy. Stop if pace deteriorates, RPE exceeds 8/10 or mechanics change. Check symptoms after sitting and the next morning."
    },
